        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0f54d04d-4492-58e3-9c2d-1fc822eb76d5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Georg F. von Tiesenhausen, Wernher von Braun\n- Events: Operation Paperclip, World War II\n- Organizations: Joint Intelligence Objectives Agency\n- Topics: Rocket science, German scientists in U.S. government employment\n\nFacts:\n- Georg F. von Tiesenhausen was born on May 18, 1914.\n- Georg F. von Tiesenhausen is a retired German-American rocket scientist.\n- At the end of World War II, Operation Paperclip was a secret program of the Joint Intelligence Objectives Agency.\n- Operation Paperclip recruited more than 1,600 German scientists, engineers, and technicians from post-Nazi Germany for U.S. government employment.\n- Wernher von Braun and his V-2 rocket team were among the people recruited by Operation Paperclip.\n- Many Operation Paperclip recruits were members of the Nazi Party, and some were Nazi Party leaders.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
